# Backup Before Edit

Before editing **any** file, first create a `.bak` copy of the original.

## The Rule

```
BEFORE editing foo/bar.py  →  copy foo/bar.py  to  foo/bar.py.bak
BEFORE editing a/b.html   →  copy a/b.html    to  a/b.html.bak
```

- The `.bak` file stays alongside the original for as long as the original exists.
- It provides an instant local revert without touching git.
- This applies to every file type: `.py`, `.html`, `.js`, `.css`, `.md`, etc.

## How to Do It

Use a Shell copy command before making any edits:

```powershell
Copy-Item "path\to\file.ext" "path\to\file.ext.bak"
```

## What NOT to Do

- Do NOT edit a file without making the `.bak` copy first.
- Do NOT delete `.bak` files unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do NOT add `.bak` to `.gitignore` — `.bak` files are committed to the repo and stay alongside their originals permanently.
